# =====================================================================
# Sentinel OS — what must never leave this machine.
# =====================================================================

# The evidence store. Raw received records, captures, and working files.
# The database holds METADATA about these; the files themselves stay local
# and are never pushed to a remote.
/evidence/*
!/evidence/.gitkeep
!/evidence/README.md
Received_Records/
manifests/

# Secrets. Never commit a real .env — config/local.example.env is the template.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.local.env
local.env

# Provenance ledgers and run captures are operator evidence, not source.
*.jsonl
qa-evidence/
builds/

# Backups and database dumps.
*.sql.gz
*.dump
pre_live_backup_*.sql
*_backup_*.sql

# Dependencies and build output.
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
tsr_env/
.next/
dist/

# =====================================================================
# Raw media. The photo library lives BESIDE this repo, never inside it.
#
# Two reasons, and the second is the one that bites:
#
#   1. Gigabytes of originals in git history make the repo unclonable and
#      can never be made smaller. History is forever — that is the same
#      argument docs/VISUAL_POLICY.md makes about private repos.
#   2. A phone photo carries EXIF GPS. Committing one publishes the exact
#      coordinates it was taken at to anyone who ever gets the repo,
#      including a future public fork. The manifest records GPS on
#      purpose and never renders it into a frame; git would do neither.
#
# The provenance does not depend on the bytes being here. Every build
# manifest hashes each input it read, so an episode can be verified
# against a library kept anywhere.
#
# To include one specific cleared image an episode genuinely needs:
#   git add -f modules/openmontage/episodes/epNN/assets/that-one.jpg
# =====================================================================
modules/openmontage/episodes/*/assets/*
!modules/openmontage/episodes/*/assets/.gitkeep
visual_manifest.json
*.photoslibrary/

# Camera and screen-recording formats, wherever they land.
*.heic
*.heif
*.mov
*.mp4
*.m4v
*.avi
*.mkv
*.mts
*.m2ts
*.dng
*.raw
*.cr2
*.nef
*.arw

# OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Your subjects of interest are not something to publish.
watchlist.json

# =====================================================================
# Bulk data and derived output.
#
# The media rules above are right that history is forever, and that
# reasoning was never applied to the corpora or to generated graph data.
# library/ (2.4 GB), shelf/ (1.0 GB) and the edge lists (133 MB) were
# untracked but NOT ignored, which is one `git add -A` from permanent.
#
# Ignoring is reversible; committing is not. Under uncertainty, ignore.
# =====================================================================
/library/
/shelf/
/inventory_out/
/_recovery/
/runs/
/anomalies/
/investigations/

# Derived graph output — regenerated by modules/connectors/edges.js from
# the corpora above. A committed copy can silently disagree with its
# generator, and then there are two answers to "what are the edges".
edges.csv
edges_israel.csv
edges.exhibits.json
nexus.csv
nexus.dot
crosscheck.csv

# Loose working files at the repo root: research inputs and outputs, not
# source. Anything here that IS source belongs under modules/ or scripts/
# and gets committed from there, deliberately, one file at a time.
/*.txt
/*.pdf
/cards.json
/hb33.json
/negev_990.json
/husted_orgs.csv
!/requirements.txt
!/README.txt
